    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0404" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg394"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Lord Russell.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-03-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 18, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> I have the honor to submit to your
                    consideration the copy of a letter addressed to me by Mr. Morse, the consul of
                    the United States at this port, relative to another war vessel, lately belonging
                    to her Majesty’s government, which is fitting out under suspicious
                    circumstances.</p>
                <p>I pray your lordship to accept the assurances of the highest consideration with
                    which I have the honor to be, my lord, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earl Russell,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>




